#
# prima-materia — the procedure judged by its own working, examined
#
# The statement at pmc:ProcedureJudgedByItsOwnWorking stood at the head of
# queries/untested-generalizations.rq on 2026-10-19 with four witnesses and no
# protocol. Its falsifier names the shape to look for: a transmission that
# compares two of its own procedures for how well they work and grounds the
# comparison in the persons who work them. This protocol puts that to the
# holding first, as SPEC §16 requires, reopens the one node the scan found in
# that shape, and opens one work outside the holding where a practitioner
# sorts the arts of his own field.
#

pmp:ProcedureJudgedByItsOwnWorkingExamination a pm:Testing ;
    rdfs:label "Whether a transmission comparing its procedures for how well they work grounds the comparison in the procedure and not in the persons"@en, "Ob eine Überlieferung, die ihre Verfahren nach ihrem Arbeiten vergleicht, den Vergleich im Verfahren begründet und nicht in den Personen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A protocol on the claim that where a transmission runs more than one procedure of the same kind and states a comparative judgement of how well they work, the ground it gives is a property of the procedure and not of the persons who work it. The population is every comparative judgement of working between procedures of one kind that a node of the holding carries in the transmission's own wording, on main on 2026-10-19 with the two nodes entered by this protocol; excluded are rankings by dignity or metaphysical order, which the statement already excludes, rankings of persons or of outcomes in persons where no two procedures are compared, and judgements made by the compiler in a note. Drawn by a scan of the English labels, definitions and notes of every node with pm:withinTradition in the compiled graph for better, best, inferior, superior, surest, more and most reliable, esteemed, easier, preferred, stronger, weaker, more and most powerful and effective, lower, highest, lowest, worse, worst, trustworthy, unreliable, liar, cheat, more certain, safer, quicker, faster and slower, 362 nodes; every hit read at the node and the judgements so found read in full. Read at the wording for this protocol: the Mahānirvāṇa Tantra reopened at X.200-204 in three versions, and Artemidorus, Onirocriticon II.69, in Greek, German and Latin, both named in examinations/searches-procedure-judged-by-its-own-working.ttl."@en ;
    pm:tests pmc:ProcedureJudgedByItsOwnWorking ;
    pm:falsifiedBy "As the statement names it: a transmission that compares two of its own procedures for how well they work and grounds the comparison in the persons who work them, that one instrument is less reliable because the men who handle it are of bad descent, impure or less well initiated. Met once in full, at the Mahānirvāṇa Tantra, which compares the receiving of the mantra from a giver of each disposition by what it produces in the receiver and grounds the difference in the disposition of the giver alone (pmc:KaulaAboveTheOtherWays, X.200-203). Met in part at Artemidorus, who sorts nine arts of divination as false and six as true and grounds the falsity jointly in the arts and in their practitioners' ignorance and deceit (pmc:ArtemidorusManteisMeApateones). Not met at any of the nineteen other judgements in the count that state a ground."@en ;
    pm:examinationState pm:casesWithDeviation ;
    pm:baseRate "Twenty-six comparative judgements of working between procedures of one kind in eighteen traditions of the holding on 2026-10-19. Seventeen give a ground that is a property of the procedure, its instrument, route, substance or record: the Zande rubbing-board, the Andean fire-readers, the Lakota exits of a disease, Zosimos's two grades, the Caraka's hut against sun and wind, Ge Hong's mysterious One against the true One, the Kālikāpurāṇa's two methods, the second verse of the Sāṃkhyakārikā, the Tzava'at ha-Rivash on joy against mortification, the Rasārṇava's ranking of digestions, the Rasa-Jala-Nidhi on the written and the oral part, the Visuddhimagga on two creations in one place, Karsten's two drinks, the Lower Congo's charms judged by the outcome, Hávamál on asking and offering, Zhu Xi on sitting against racing about, and the demotic papyrus's marks of trial. One grounds it in the operator's state during the act, the Tzava'at ha-Rivash on prayer with an alien thought against silence. One grounds it in a pedigree, the demotic papyrus's feat of King Darius than which there is nothing better. One grounds it in the persons who work the procedure, the Mahānirvāṇa Tantra on the givers of the mantra. One grounds it in procedure and persons together, Artemidorus on the arts of divination. Five state the judgement and no ground: the Rasa-Jala-Nidhi's best process of swooning and its preferred black mercury, the Caraka's best manner of taking emblic, the Zhen'gao's highest method of transcendence, and the Tzava'at ha-Rivash on prayer without motion."@en ;
    pm:counterSearch pm:counterSearchFoundOpposition ;
    pm:counterSearchNote "Searched: the compiled holding as of 2026-10-19 on main, by the scan in the definition; read at the node, besides the four witnesses: pmc:AyurvedaKutipravesika, pmc:AyurvedaKutyadhikarin, pmc:AyurvedaAmalakarasayanaCaturtha, pmc:Fenxing, pmc:HeterodoxWorshipNeverClearsTheDebt, pmc:SamkhyaAnusravikaAvisuddhi, pmc:HasidismTaanitEinayim, pmc:HasidismKlipaRochevet, pmc:HasidismSimanimShelDevekut, pmc:RasarnavaJirnarasabhaksana, pmc:RasaGuptavidya, pmc:RasaMurchana, pmc:RasaKhecaratva, pmc:TirokuddaGamana, pmc:JibaroMaikoaUmartinyu, pmc:WhatMayBeDoubtedAndWhatMayNot, pmc:NorseOfblotit, pmc:ZhuziYifaDispute, pmc:PdmProbatumNovies, pmc:PdmGratiaAnteOmnes, pmc:ShangqingZhoushiSanxiong, pmc:KaulaAboveTheOtherWays, pmc:AcaraLadder, pmc:FivefoldPrimaryRasaRanking, pmc:JainaTrividhamaranakrama, pmc:ShangqingShijieZhengbian, pmc:CmSandeThreeGrades, pmc:JainaSakamamaranaNaSarvesham, pmc:CautionAgainstOperatingAcrossTheSexes, pmc:TaulipangLongerStudyStrongerShaman, pmc:VoSisa, pmc:CmLibuweishi, pmc:AnapanasatiDukkara, pmc:ClaviculaFurisVisio, pmc:FabricationRatherThanMisreport, pmc:FraudKnownAndBeliefHeld. Read at the wording outside the holding: Mahānirvāṇa Tantra X.198-207 in Avalon, in the Calcutta Sanskrit of 1884 and in a second English translation, with XIV.167-211 in Avalon; Artemidorus II.68-70 in Hercher's Greek, Krauss's German and Cornarius's Latin. Found for the statement: no new witness; the seventeen judgements with a procedural ground include the four witnesses and thirteen that were in the holding and not set beside them. Found against it: the full falsifier once, at a node whose locus had been wrong and which now stands at X.203, and the falsifier in part once, in the work opened. Not searched: the commentary of Hariharānanda on X.203, the other works of the Śaiva and Śākta corpus on the choice of a guru, and the rest of the Onirocriticon; and the scan is lexical over English wording, so a comparison worded without a comparative is not in the count."@en ;
    pm:examinedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-19" ;
    pm:protocolUpdated "2026-10-19" ;
    skos:note "The statement fails as a rule and survives with a condition that the cases supply. Every judgement in the count whose ground names a person compares procedures that are told apart by a person: the mantra from this giver or that, the arts of this kind of diviner or that, the feat of this king. Every judgement whose ground is the procedure compares procedures that are told apart by what is done: the instrument, the route, the substance, the length, the order in time. The ground follows whatever distinguishes the two things compared. The statement is rewritten at the node to say so, with the old wording kept in a note."@en ;
    skos:note "That makes half of the rewritten statement nearly analytic, and the protocol says so rather than claiming a finding there. A comparison has to be grounded in something that differs between what it compares, and if two procedures differ only in what is done, a ground in the persons is not available to it. What is not analytic is the other half: that a transmission which runs a procedure told apart by its giver, an initiation, grounds its working in the giver and not in the rite. The Mahānirvāṇa Tantra does exactly that; it names nothing the giver does, and the receiver becomes what the giver is. That is a claim about initiation and it is the next thing to examine, against the descent of power in the same file (pmc:Saktipata), which grades the giving and not the giver."@en ;
    skos:note "A boundary the population leaves out and the reader should not lose. Where the holding compares operators of one procedure rather than procedures, it grounds the comparison in the operator without exception in the nodes read: women are to magnetise women, for a man cannot employ the processes best calculated to soothe them; the longer the Taulipang study lasts, the stronger the Zauberarzt; the Lower Congo villagers send for the stranger because they see that their own man's charms cannot keep his household; the Celestial Masters lay a failed cure on the officiant's want of competence. The statement was formed in a way that excluded these, and this protocol keeps the exclusion; it is recorded so that the statement is not read as saying that transmissions do not blame persons."@en ;
    skos:note "The case the falsifier itself did not foresee is the operator's state during the act. The Tzava'at ha-Rivash judges prayer with an alien thought worse than silence, for the shell rides on the speech. The ground is neither a standing property of a person, as descent or initiation would be, nor a property of what is done, since the words are the same; it is the condition in which the same thing is done. Counted apart, as one case, and not as a deviation."@en ;
    skos:note "What the reopened node changes beyond this protocol. pmc:KaulaAboveTheOtherWays cited Mahānirvāṇa Tantra XIV.203 for the claim about the mantra and its giver since it was written; that verse says the tantra is the only means for the knowledge of Brahman, and the claim stands at X.203. The node now names the right verse, three versions of it, and the work; traditions/saiva-sakta.ttl was migrated to work identifiers in the same run because it was touched."@en .
